.TH btctax-income-scrub 1  btctax "btctax manual"
.SH NAME
scrub \- Write a SHAREABLE copy of this year\*(Aqs inputs: every figure preserved, the identity replaced
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBscrub\fR <\fB\-\-year\fR> [\fB\-\-out\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Write a SHAREABLE copy of this year\*(Aqs inputs: every figure preserved, the identity replaced.
.PP
For handing a real return to someone else — a maintainer, a reviewer — so they can reproduce a refusal or a wrong figure without receiving your PII. Names, SSNs, the address, employer and payer names are replaced with synthetic stand\-ins; the IP PIN is DROPPED, never faked, because a plausible\-looking one in a file marked safe to share is worse than none.
.PP
Everything the computation reads survives unchanged: every dollar figure, the filing status, dates of birth and death, blindness, the dependent count and each relationship, and every fail\-loud declaration. W\-2 EINs are replaced but keep their SAMENESS, because §6413(c)\*(Aqs excess\-social\-security credit turns on having more than one employer.
.PP
Every computed FIGURE is preserved — a guarantee held by `scrub_preserves_every_computed_figure`, which compares the whole assembled return, not a sampled line.
.PP
It does NOT compute an identical return in every respect, and here is the whole list of what differs. Four things are REPLACED and still printed on a form: the Schedule C business description (line A, and Form 8995\-A line 1(a)), the foreign\-account country list (Schedule B line 7b), and the interest and dividend payer names (Schedule B Parts I and II). Two more change a MESSAGE rather than a page: the broker name inside a Form 1099\-B refusal, and the employer EIN inside the excess\-social\-security advisory. One is DROPPED rather than replaced, so its box goes blank: the IP PIN. And a cross\-year advisory will not fire, because the copy carries one year.
.PP
With \-\-out the file is written owner\-only (0600). Without it the TOML goes to stdout, and a shell redirect creates the file at your umask — usually world\-readable — so prefer \-\-out for anything you keep.
.PP
Either way the output carries a marker line, so a plain `income import` refuses it; load it with `income import \-\-force`, ideally into a scratch vault.
.PP
What it is NOT is anonymous: the figures alone are a financial profile. Do not round or fuzz them to compensate; crossing a bracket, a phase\-out or the standard\-vs\-itemized line changes the behaviour you are trying to show.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-year\fR \fI<YEAR>\fR
The tax year (e.g. 2024)
.TP
\fB\-\-out\fR \fI<OUT>\fR
Write here instead of stdout
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
